.TH LINKWISE 1 "2026-11-13" "Linkwise" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linkwise \- operate the Linkwise modem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkwise
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.br
.B linkwise encode-frame
.I level control input output
.RI [ format ]
.br
.B linkwise transmit-frame
.I level control input
.br
.B linkwise decode-frame
.I input
.br
.B linkwise send
.I source destination input
.RI [ "command-port data-port" ]
.br
.B linkwise mail queue
.I mailbox envelope
.br
.B linkwise mail smtp
.I mailbox callsign
.RI [ port ]
.br
.B linkwise mail imap
.I mailbox
.RI [ port ]
.br
.B linkwise mail
.RI { exchange | listen }
.I mailbox local peer
.RI [ "command-port data-port" ]
.br
.B linkwise secure
.RI { send | receive }
.I config file
.br
.B linkwise
.RI { analyze-wav | decode-wav }
.I input
.br
.B linkwise render-wav
.I request-json output-wav
.br
.B linkwise
.RI { audio-inputs | audio-outputs }
.br
.B linkwise receive-audio
.I seconds
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments, start the MCP server on standard input and output.
An optional
.B \-\-
before command operands ends option parsing.
A path written as
.B ./-
refers to a literal file named
.BR - .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode-frame
Render a single BW500 DATA frame to a file or standard output.
Levels 1, 2, and 3 require exactly 9, 22, and 34 payload bytes, respectively.
Supply a control byte in decimal or hexadecimal with a
.B 0x
prefix.
Input and output accept
.B -
for standard input and output.
The default format is WAV. Specify
.B pcm-f32le
for raw little-endian IEEE float samples.
Both formats use 48 kHz, mono, 32-bit samples.
A named output file is overwritten after input validation.
.TP
.B transmit-frame
Encode the same DATA frame and play it on the selected output device.
Requires an audio-enabled build. This command generates audio without
controlling PTT. Success means the device's presentation estimate elapsed.
.TP
.B decode-frame
Read a 48 kHz mono WAV and write the payload of exactly one CRC-valid
DATA frame as binary stdout. Zero or multiple frames produce an error.
.TP
.B send
Open a P2P session through the local modem command and data ports.
Send bytes from a file or standard input and wait for the modem to
acknowledge the transmit queue and report disconnection.
The default ports are 8300 and 8301.
Both custom ports must be supplied together.
The source callsign must match the configured station.
This command consumes inbound data to keep the transport flowing.
.TP
.B mail queue
Queue a Winlink B2F envelope of up to 1 MiB in a private mailbox directory.
Use a local filesystem with hard-link support.
.TP
.B mail smtp
Accept local SMTP submissions and queue them for B2F peer-to-peer forwarding.
The listener binds to IPv4 loopback and defaults to port 2525.
With the mail-tls build feature, append
.B PORT --tls CERT.pem KEY.pem
for implicit TLS or
.B PORT --starttls CERT.pem KEY.pem
for SMTP STARTTLS.
Set both
.B LINKWISE_SMTP_USER
and
.B LINKWISE_SMTP_PASSWORD
to require AUTH LOGIN after TLS.
The authenticated account can submit only as the configured station.
.TP
.B mail imap
Expose a read-only inbox over local IMAP.
The listener binds to IPv4 loopback and defaults to port 1143.
With the mail-tls build feature, append
.B PORT --tls CERT.pem KEY.pem
to use implicit TLS.
Local connections are automatically authenticated by default.
Set both
.B LINKWISE_IMAP_USER
and
.B LINKWISE_IMAP_PASSWORD
to require IMAP LOGIN over TLS.
Select the inbox or poll with NOOP to discover newly received mail.
Message UIDs stay stable until the listener restarts.
.TP
.B mail exchange, mail listen
Call a peer or listen for a specified peer through the local modem.
Exchange queued and incoming B2F messages in one session.
The default loopback command and data ports are 8300 and 8301.
Supply both port overrides together.
Run one exchange at a time per mailbox.
Incoming envelopes are stored under
.B inbox
using the lowercase hexadecimal encoding of the message ID as the filename,
with a
.B .b2f
suffix.
Success requires B2F termination and a modem disconnection notice.
.TP
.B secure send, secure receive
Transfer one payload between two Linkwise peers using mutual TLS 1.3
with 256-bit AES-GCM traffic keys.
Requires a source build with the
.B secure-transfer
feature. Standard modem installers omit this feature.
Both peers require a separate JSON configuration with
.B encryption.enabled
set to
.BR true .
The default is disabled. The configuration specifies local and peer
callsigns, loopback command and data ports, certificates, and a size limit.
The receiver checks the byte count and SHA-256 digest before publishing
a named file and refuses to overwrite an existing file.
The sender checks the authenticated receipt.
Both commands wait for the modem to report disconnection
before returning success.
See the encrypted P2P transfer guide in the source tree
.RI (rust/docs/secure-transfer.md)
for the configuration format and certificate setup.
.TP
.B analyze-wav
Report burst candidates as a JSON object.
.TP
.B decode-wav
Report burst candidates and CRC-valid DATA frames as a JSON object.
Each frame includes its level, sample range, payload in hexadecimal,
and control byte. Both WAV commands accept
.B -
for stdin and support 16-bit PCM and 32-bit float mono WAV input.
Decoding requires 48 kHz.
.TP
.B render-wav
Render a BW500 handshake stimulus from a JSON file to a WAV file.
Write a JSON summary to stdout.
.TP
.B audio-inputs, audio-outputs
List native audio device names as JSON arrays.
.TP
.B receive-audio
Receive for 1 to 3600 seconds. Write one JSON object per burst candidate,
with an array of decoded frames. Each frame includes its control byte.
.SH STANDARD STREAMS
Frame payloads and waveforms use binary streams. Reports use JSON.
Diagnostics go to standard error.
For a frame input, EOF ends the payload and an empty, short, or oversized
payload fails before encoding or playback.
For
.BR send ,
EOF ends the transfer. Empty input succeeds without opening a session.
For
.BR "secure send" ,
a file operand of
.B -
reads standard input. For
.BR "secure receive" ,
it writes binary standard output, which may contain partial data if the
transfer fails.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LINKWISE_AUDIO_INPUT
Exact input device name. Defaults to the system input.
.TP
.B LINKWISE_AUDIO_CHANNEL
Zero-based input channel. Defaults to 0.
.TP
.B LINKWISE_AUDIO_OUTPUT
Exact output device name. Required for
.BR transmit-frame .
.TP
.B LINKWISE_AUDIO_OUTPUT_CHANNEL
Zero-based output channel. Defaults to 0.
.TP
.B LINKWISE_BW500_PROFILE
Optional level 4 measurement profile for decoding. Required for rendering
a BW500 setup stimulus.
.TP
.B LINKWISE_RADIO_BACKEND
MCP radio backend. Defaults to
.BR simulated .
Set to
.B rigctld
to use Hamlib.
.TP
.B LINKWISE_RIGCTLD_ADDR
MCP rigctld endpoint. Defaults to
.BR hamlib:4532 .
.TP
.B LINKWISE_RADIO_WRITES
Enable MCP radio writes with
.BR true .
Requires station limits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The selected operation completed.
.TP
.B 1
The operation failed, including I/O errors and a closed output pipe.
.TP
.B 2
The command or its operands were invalid, or the build lacks
secure transfer support.
.TP
.B 130
A live send, transmit, or receive command was interrupted by SIGINT
or by Ctrl-C or Ctrl-Break on Windows.
.TP
.B 143
A live command was interrupted by SIGTERM on Unix.
.SH SIGNALS
An interrupted send closes both modem sockets.
Delivery of bytes still awaiting acknowledgment is uncertain.
For a secure transfer, the receiver may already have published the file
if the session ends before the sender obtains the receipt.
Interrupting live audio releases the device.
A closed stdout pipe causes a quiet output failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Round trip without a radio
Create a nine-byte payload that includes a NUL byte. Write a WAV and
verify that decoding recovers the exact input.
.EX
printf '\e00012345678' >payload.bin
linkwise encode-frame 1 0xa5 payload.bin tx.wav
linkwise decode-frame tx.wav >received.bin
cmp payload.bin received.bin
.EE
.SS Pipe the waveform and redirect diagnostics
.EX
linkwise encode-frame 1 0xa5 - - <payload.bin 2>encode.log |
    linkwise decode-frame - >received.bin 2>decode.log
cmp payload.bin received.bin
.EE
.SS Inspect the decoded control byte
.EX
linkwise decode-wav tx.wav | jq '.bw500_data_frames[].control'
.EE
.SS Play a frame through an isolated audio device
Use the exact name reported by
.BR audio-outputs .
.EX
linkwise audio-outputs
LINKWISE_AUDIO_OUTPUT='Loopback Device' \\
    linkwise transmit-frame 1 0xa5 - <payload.bin
.EE
.SS Send a file through the running modem
Replace the callsigns with your configured source and intended peer.
.EX
linkwise send W1AW K1ABC message.bin 2>send.log
.EE
.SS Exchange queued Winlink mail
.nf
linkwise mail queue ./mailbox message.b2f
linkwise mail exchange ./mailbox N0CALL W1AW
.fi
.SS Send an encrypted file
Using secure-enabled builds, start the first command on the receiving
station and the second on the sending station. The two JSON files
contain the respective station's secure transfer settings.
.EX
linkwise secure receive receiver.json received.bin
linkwise secure send sender.json original.bin 2>secure-send.log
.EE
.SS Read an encrypted transfer payload from standard input
With the receiver listening, use shell input redirection to send a file.
.EX
linkwise secure send sender.json - <original.bin
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linkwise-modemd (8),
.BR linkwise-station (5)
